{
  "requirement": "Every call constructs a fresh `ValidationContext` identifying the source node\nand calls `Criterion::execute` with that context. Its completed answer, including\na negative assessment, and captured dependencies form the returned `Fingerprinted`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.inputs`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.validate_node`. I derived four obligations from its text and mapped each to a test.\n\n1. **A fresh `ValidationContext` per call, identifying the source node.**\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces]` runs three concurrent verifications. The test criterion's `execute` reads and lists edges of its own context's node. The test asserts that each stored record's dependencies hold only that node's content and edge observations (`Node(n)` and `OutgoingEdges(n, 1, ..)`). The test peaks at 3 in-flight executions, so the contexts were separate and each was bound to the correct source node.\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[historical_freshness_reads_do_not_enter_the_replacement_trace]` calls `load_evidence` and `check_inputs` on the same validator before `verify`. `check_inputs` reads node 2. The replacement record still holds only `Node(1, root)`, so the new context starts empty and does not inherit earlier observations.\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` runs two concurrent agent executions on the same node and criterion. It asserts that their dependency traces (alpha: only node 1; beta: node 1's edges and node 2) and their usage counters stay separate.\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations]` asserts that the stored dependencies after execution contain only the execution's own read, `Node(2)` with content \"after\".\n\n2. **`Criterion::execute` is called with that context.**\n   - The test criteria (`Review` in `validation_tests.rs` and `contracts.rs`) do all their reading and listing through the `cx` passed to `execute`.\n   - Assertions on the resulting dependencies, and on `executions` counts (for example 1 and 0 writes, and 2 in the input-checking test), show that `execute` ran with the supplied context.\n\n3. **The completed answer, including a negative assessment, forms the output.**\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` verifies a negative typed answer and asserts `value.output() == &negative`. It also asserts the source node, the criterion path and the version.\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]` asserts `!value.output().result` for a negative answer.\n\n4. **Captured dependencies form the returned `Fingerprinted`.**\n   - `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` asserts `value.dependencies().is_empty()` for a criterion that reads nothing.\n   - The concurrent test and the agent tests assert nonempty dependencies. These cover node reads, outgoing-edge selections, and tool-driven observations. The assertions are on the stored records and on `result.dependencies()`.\n   - `changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another` and `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations` assert the exact captured dependency fingerprints.\n\nThe `{cite}` of `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.inputs` needs no separate coverage here. Its accessor and ownership behavior is exercised through the same tests. I found no gap I can state as requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept, and I found no marking gap.",
  "references": "7efd14ac6912ec5776950f4b6750f8003a698e0519b38e57e5cc03ae8ed8463f",
